{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/755732-mystery-cult-initiation-aves-minerva-sas-paterfamilias","id":755732,"title":"Mystery Cult Initiation : Aves Minerva (SAS: Paterfamilias)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-04T20:13:06-08:00","id":755732,"title":"Mystery Cult Initiation : Aves Minerva (SAS: Paterfamilias)","content":"I've been recently particularly interested with the Birds of Minerva organization in Requiem for Rome. I hadn't recalled seeing any attempts at revising the merit from VtR v1 up to 2.0, so I took a stab at it, and turned it into a Mystery Cult Initiation.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Mystery Cult Initiation: </i>Aves Minervae</b><br /> <br /> A secretive organization who operate in secret in the height of Empire, the Birds consider themselves emissaries of their goddess, Minerva. Trained to notice the telltale signs of the hungry dead and the cold shadows that fill Rome's nights, they are blessed with the means and knowledge to dispatch these creatures in Rome's service. Their purpose, relics, and doctrine are described in the SAS <i>Paterfamilias</i> in greater detail.<br /> <br /> <b>Benefits</b><br /> O - The first step in knowing of the presence of monsters around you is knowing your environment and its inhabitants in greater detail. Members gain the <i>Trained Observer </i>merit at one dot, so long as they satisfy the prerequisites.<br /> OO - The <i>aves</i> is initiated into some of the Red Rituals, granting them the <i>Endowments [Aves Minerva] </i>merit at one dot. If they choose to purchase more with experience, they may add the dots together.<br /> OOO - Greater knowledge of the <i>lemures</i> and <i>manes</i> that inhabit Rome's catacombs and dark corners gives an almost instinctive knowledge of their mere presence. Members gain the <i>Unseen Sense</i> merit, applying to Kindred and Strix (as they are essentially similar enough).<br /> OOOO - Further initiation into the Red Rituals grants the <i>aves</i> a second dot in <i>Endowments [Aves Minerva]</i>.<br /> OOOOO - The most high-ranked and experienced members of the Birds of Minerva have amassed a great deal of knowledge on the <i>di inferi</i>. A member at this status gains five dots in the <i>Library</i> merit, to be divided up into relevant information: Academics, Occult, and Religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 11-05-2015, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T08:26:17-08:00","id":756606,"title":"","content":"What about the Endowment and the Red Rituals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T09:13:35-08:00","id":756659,"title":"","content":"Mystery Cult Initiation is not a Hunter thing-it doesn't have Endowments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T09:45:13-08:00","id":756691,"title":"","content":"I assumed they were the precursors of the Cainite Heresy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T10:17:19-08:00","id":756713,"title":"","content":"Did you not see the 2nd dot?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> OO - The <i>aves</i> is initiated into some of the Red Rituals, granting them the Endowments [Aves Minerva] merit at one dot. If they choose to purchase more with experience, they may add the dots together. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T10:31:41-08:00","id":756833,"title":"","content":"well, there seem to be a movement among the homebrew of representing compacts/conspiracies as Mystery Cults- not that I've done it, but I've saw some people who chose to use the Cult as a module for a 2nd edition Hunter orgs. Considering that for now there is nothing official about how (if?) the Status bonus would change on the new edition, I think that both methods are valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T11:51:33-08:00","id":757036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/755732-mystery-cult-initiation-aves-minerva-sas-paterfamilias?p=756691#post756691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed they were the precursors of the Cainite Heresy.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the lore from the SAS, I believe that's actually one fate for the Birds after the fall of Rome: they fall apart, but the rituals are passed on (in a modified format in the modern era).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/755732-mystery-cult-initiation-aves-minerva-sas-paterfamilias?p=756833#post756833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . . there seem to be a movement among the homebrew of representing compacts/conspiracies as Mystery Cults . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically why I rewrote the merit as a Mystery Cult Initiation (though I'm still looking over the Red Rituals themselves and wondering what needs updating there too): The organization has a purpose/doctrine (hunting Vampires and Strix), a relic (the font where their rituals are derived), and a set of benefits to match those things.<br /> <br /> Since Hunter/Vigil is yet to be updated (Summer 2016, maybe?), I figured this was the closest I could get to representing them . I also felt they needed some fleshing out; I always found it a little frustrating that the merit in VtR 1 only had 3 benefits while you still had to pay for 5 ranks\u2014and with the old style experience point system that made it even more cost-benefit unwieldy. (The Status you might get from the old merit would only work internally anyway, with other organization members, so it wasn't hugely influential with such a small cult.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 11-05-2015, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T12:00:47-08:00","id":757044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hunter the Vigil: Night Stalkers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our nation has abandoned Minerva; Minerva has in turn abandoned us.</div> </div> </div> </div>One member made a plea to others to join the Cainites, but it looks as if the Cainite Heresy existed parallel to the Aves, though they didn't have the power yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Brothers, I taught them the first of the Red Rituals: The Denials. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T12:34:07-08:00","id":774197,"title":"","content":"Are the Red rituals the same as the rituals of Denial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T17:32:49-08:00","id":774406,"title":"","content":"The quote suggests that the Rituals of Denial are the 'first' of the Red Rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}